    "# The  the difference between for and while loops. Give an example of each.\n",
    "\n",
    "# A for loop is for iterating through a sequence (like a list, a string, or a range of numbers). We use it when we know how many times we want to loop. It's like saying, \"Do this for every item on my list.\"\n",
    "# A while loop is for looping as long as a certain condition is True. We use it when we don't know how many times we will need to loop. It's like saying, \"Keep doing this until I tell you to stop.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# for loop example:\n",
    "\n",
    "# This will loop exactly 5 times, for each name in the list.\n",
    "names = [\"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\", \"David\", \"Eve\"]\n",
    "for name in names:\n",
    "    print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# while loop example:\n",
    "\n",
    "# This will keep looping until the number is no longer less than 5.\n",
    "number = 0\n",
    "while number < 5:\n",
    "    print(f\"The number is now {number}\")\n",
    "    number = number + 1 # It's crucial to change the condition inside the loop!"
   ]
